  <prompt>SPLIT-MODE EXECUTION (amended 2026-08-18 per owner decision). This task now executes in two halves: (1) a scaffolding-only subagent authors the verification harness, report skeleton, and operator runbook (this half — see notes/phase-f-verification-harness.md, notes/phase-f-report-skeleton.md, notes/phase-f-operator-runbook.md); (2) the owner (interactive main-session, real AAD identity) invokes /provision-environment against dev to actually provision the stamp and fills the report. The subagent half MUST NOT invoke /provision-environment or mutate any live Azure/Dataverse resource. Per spec.md FR-18 + SC #5 + design.md §15 + the 2026-08-18 Path A exception (see &lt;constraints&gt;): provision a fresh trial-{yyyymmdd} customer stamp using the Model 2 (dedicated) profile via the new pipeline invoked through /provision-environment skill. Verify: (a) Setup Status transitions to Ready; (b) all 6 §4B silent-fail traps (T1-T6) cleared by owning handler post-conditions; (c) all 5 §4D tenant-isolation invariants (I1-I5) sample-verified; (d) scripts/naming-conformance-check.ps1 exits 0 on r1-owned surfaces; (e) cost envelope conforms per §15 #14 targets (Model 2 empty-environment Azure floor ≤ $400/mo); (f) Model 1/2 handler behavior differences per §4.1a verified (Model 2 dry-run/full-run mandatory; Model 1 discretionary). Publish full E2E verification report at projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/phase-f-e2e-acceptance-2026-08-18.md (owner fills from the skeleton at notes/phase-f-report-skeleton.md).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform senior engineer + operator. Expert in the full 19-handler pipeline (H0..H14), L2 REST + reconciler operation, §4B trap catalog + §4D invariant enforcement, cost envelope measurement via Azure Cost Management, and E2E verification-report authoring. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>A fresh trial-{yyyymmdd} customer stamp exists in dev Azure with Model 2 (dedicated) profile; Setup Status = Ready in Dataverse; all 6 §4B traps verified cleared; all 5 §4D invariants sample-verified; naming-conformance-check.ps1 exits 0; cost envelope report shows conformance to §15 #14 targets. Verification report at projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/phase-f-e2e-acceptance-2026-08-18.md documents every check + verdict + supporting evidence. SCAFFOLDING HALF (this dispatch) delivers the verification harness, report skeleton, and operator runbook that make the owner's live invocation mechanical and auditable; it does not itself produce the live evidence.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Per spec.md FR-18 + SC #5 + design.md §15 north-star + plan.md Phase F: this is the project's final acceptance gate. Fresh trial-{yyyymmdd} customer using Model 2 (dedicated) profile invoked via the L3 /provision-environment skill (task 075) exercises the entire pipeline end-to-end, including the dedicated-stamp code paths (fresh App Service, fresh OpenAI, fresh AI Search, H0.5 consent-callback) that carry the highest first-live-run surprise probability. Trap + invariant + naming + cost verification confirms the pipeline delivers a customer environment that meets binding acceptance criteria. Any failure blocks project completion (task 090). SPLIT APPROACH (2026-08-18): a scaffolding-only subagent (Sub-Agent Write Boundary-compliant; does not invoke /provision-environment or touch live Azure/Dataverse) authors the verification harness + report skeleton + operator runbook; the owner performs the actual live invocation interactively and fills in the report from the skeleton.</background>
