  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-18">SCOPE: H13 acceptance gate exits 0 AND registry Setup Status = Ready; both required.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md SC #5">SCOPE: E2E acceptance target = trial-{yyyymmdd} Model 1 stamp reaches Ready via new pipeline (not manual invocation).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md SC #6">SCOPE: All 6 §4B T1-T6 traps verified cleared by owning handler post-conditions.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md §4D">SCOPE: All 5 I1-I5 invariants sample-verified — I1 (no hardcoded tenant), I2 (tenantId filter on AI Search), I3 (Cosmos partition key), I4 (SPE container-id resolver), I5 (Graph per-tenant token).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-35">SCOPE: naming-conformance-check.ps1 exits 0 on r1-owned surfaces post-provisioning.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md §15 #14">SCOPE: Cost envelope — Model 2 empty-environment Azure floor ≤ $400/mo (primary path); Model 1 marginal ≤ $430/mo + shared platform floor ≤ $400/mo (if Model 1 discretionary run performed); deviations &gt;20% flagged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-§10">SCOPE: If E2E surfaces a BFF issue, remediation follows §10 BFF Hygiene; /conflict-check before any fix PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: E2E provisioning uses REAL L3 skill invocation via /provision-environment against dev L2 — NOT a scripted bypass. Skill invocation is the acceptance path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE (AMENDED 2026-08-18): Model 2 (dedicated) full-run is now MANDATORY as the primary acceptance path (customerId=trial-2026-08-18, tenancyModel=Model2Dedicated, profile=trial). Model 1 dry-run is now discretionary; document Model 1 result or explicit skip rationale if not performed. This is the inverse of the original mandatoriness assignment — see the Path A exception constraint below for rationale.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-§6.5">ADR Tension / Path A Exception (2026-08-18, owner-authorized): Path A exception: Model 2 mandatory (was discretionary); Model 1 discretionary (was mandatory). Rationale: dedicated stamp exercises fresh App Service + OpenAI + AI Search — higher first-live-run surprise probability = higher acceptance value. Documented in POML amendment 2026-08-18 per owner decision. Alternative considered (and rejected): keep Model 1 mandatory as originally scoped in plan.md §4 Phase F — rejected because Model 1 shares the already-daily-exercised platform floor (App Service Plan, AI Search, OpenAI) and would validate little that isn't already covered by ongoing dev usage; Model 2's fully-dedicated stamp (new UAMI, KV, Cosmos, Storage, dedicated App Service Plan + AI Search + OpenAI + mandatory H0.5 consent-callback) is the higher-value first real invocation of the pipeline. Impact: acceptance evidence for Model 1's shared-tier path is deferred to a discretionary run or a future customer onboarding; Model 2's dedicated-stamp path becomes the binding SC #5/#6 evidence trail for task 090 wrap-up.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE (SPLIT MODE, added 2026-08-18): This task executes in two halves. The scaffolding half (subagent, Sub-Agent Write Boundary-compliant) authors: notes/phase-f-verification-harness.md, notes/phase-f-report-skeleton.md, notes/phase-f-operator-runbook.md. It MUST NOT invoke /provision-environment, MUST NOT run any `az`/`pac`/MCP command that mutates a live Azure or Dataverse resource, and MUST NOT deploy to spaarke-bff-dev. The owner-invocation half (interactive main-session, operator's own AAD identity) runs the actual /provision-environment skill invocation per the operator runbook and fills the final report at notes/phase-f-e2e-acceptance-2026-08-18.md from the skeleton.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: If ANY trap OR invariant OR cost check fails, STOP + escalate per CLAUDE.md §6.5 rather than lowering the threshold.</constraint>
  </constraints>

