  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Load spec.md FR-18 + SC #5 + SC #6 + §4B + §4D + §15 #14 + design.md §15 + §4.1a.</step>
    <step order="0.5" name="SCAFFOLDING HALF (subagent, this dispatch)">Author notes/phase-f-verification-harness.md (per-trap T1-T6 + per-invariant I1-I5 verification queries + naming-conformance runner + cost envelope query), notes/phase-f-report-skeleton.md (owner fill-in template), notes/phase-f-operator-runbook.md (step-by-step operator commands wrapping /provision-environment). Amend this POML for the Model 1/2 mandatoriness swap. Update TASK-INDEX.md row 089 to 🟡 in-progress. Do NOT proceed past this step in the scaffolding dispatch.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Prereq check (OWNER HALF)">Verify all dep tasks (057-088) status = ✅ in TASK-INDEX.md; verify /provision-environment skill is invocable. Owner runs via operator runbook Step 1.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Model 2 provision (OWNER HALF, PRIMARY PATH)">Invoke /provision-environment with customerId=trial-2026-08-18, tenancyModel=Model2Dedicated, profile=trial. Walk through skill Step 0 → completion (H0.5 consent-callback fires — see operator runbook); capture handoff report.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Setup Status check (OWNER HALF)">Query sprk_dataverseenvironment for the trial customer; verify sprk_provisioning_setupstatus = Ready.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Trap verification (OWNER HALF)">For each of T1-T6, run the trap-verification query (per notes/phase-f-verification-harness.md, sourced from §4B) against the trial stamp; document result per trap.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Invariant verification (OWNER HALF)">Sample-verify each of I1-I5 per notes/phase-f-verification-harness.md: (I1) grep provisioning scripts for tenant-shaped defaults; (I2) sample AI Search query on the DEDICATED index; (I3) sample Cosmos query; (I4) verify SPE container-ID resolution; (I5) verify Graph token per-tenant scope.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Naming conformance (OWNER HALF)">Run `pwsh -File scripts/naming-conformance-check.ps1 -Scope r1-owned`; expect exit 0.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Cost envelope (OWNER HALF)">Query Azure Cost Management API for the trial stamp's dedicated RG; compare against §15 #14 Model 2 ≤$400/mo target.</step>
    <step order="8" name="Model 1 dry-run (OWNER HALF, now DISCRETIONARY)">Discretionary — if reasonable in dev budget, provision or dry-run a second stamp with tenancyModel=Model1Shared + verify §4.1a differences hold; else document skip rationale.</step>
    <step order="9" name="Report (OWNER HALF)">Fill notes/phase-f-report-skeleton.md into notes/phase-f-e2e-acceptance-2026-08-18.md with per-check verdict + evidence + Setup Status confirmation + cost report + Model 1 result-or-skip.</step>
    <step order="10" name="Cleanup (OWNER HALF)">Discretionary teardown OR leave trial stamp for reference (per plan.md Phase F Deliverables); see operator runbook teardown checklist.</step>
    <step order="11" name="Index update (OWNER HALF)">Update TASK-INDEX.md: task 089 → ✅ once owner invocation + report are complete.</step>
    <step order="12" name="Deviations">Document any deviation in projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If ANY trap OR ANY invariant OR cost drift &gt;20% fails, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6.5 rather than lowering the threshold or silently proceeding. Phase F acceptance is BINDING — a fail here blocks task 090 wrap-up. Owner input required on remediation path (path A exception documented; path B ADR amendment; path C fix + re-run).</trigger>
  </escalation>

